sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Platform User
    participant Client as External Client
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS
    participant DCController as dc-controller-manager<br/>(Go Operator)
    participant KRBP as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>(Sidecar)
    participant REST as REST Service<br/>(actix-web)
    participant Backend as Backend Connector<br/>(PG/ES/Milvus/Neo4j/S3/...)

    Note over User, Backend: Flow 1: DataConnectService CR Reconciliation

    User->>K8sAPI: Create/Update DataConnectService CR<br/>HTTPS/6443, TLS 1.2+, User Token
    K8sAPI-->>DCController: Watch Event<br/>TLS 1.2+, ServiceAccount
    DCController->>K8sAPI: Read OpenShift Ingress Config<br/>HTTPS/6443, TLS 1.2+
    K8sAPI-->>DCController: Cluster routing domain
    DCController->>K8sAPI: Create Deployments, Services,<br/>ConfigMaps, NetworkPolicies, HTTPRoutes<br/>HTTPS/6443, TLS 1.2+
    K8sAPI-->>DCController: Resources created

    Note over User, Backend: Flow 2: REST API Data Connection Request

    Client->>KRBP: POST /api/{version}/data/connections<br/>HTTPS, TLS 1.2+, Bearer Token
    KRBP->>K8sAPI: TokenReview<br/>HTTPS/6443, TLS 1.2+
    K8sAPI-->>KRBP: Token validated
    KRBP->>REST: Forward request<br/>HTTP (localhost), X-Tenant-ID required
    REST->>REST: validate_headers middleware<br/>Check X-Tenant-ID present
    REST->>Backend: Query/mutate data<br/>Backend-specific protocol & auth
    Backend-->>REST: Result
    REST-->>KRBP: JSON Response
    KRBP-->>Client: HTTPS Response

    Note over User, Backend: Flow 3: Connection Type Synchronization

    User->>K8sAPI: Create InitDataConnectionType CR<br/>HTTPS/6443, TLS 1.2+
    K8sAPI-->>DCController: Watch Event (IDCType CR change)
    DCController->>REST: Sync connection type definition<br/>HTTP, Internal
    REST-->>DCController: Sync result
    Note right of DCController: ConfigMap changes also trigger<br/>sync via ConfigMapWatcherReconciler
